From f3b281e1b3c9371d90928607bd55c87a21fd3962 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:06:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): external-run hover, stamps, hollow cloud, down
 label [daveey]

Review of #3744 @2da5291b requested changes. A stale next_due_at painted red while
the hover still said "<service> ok" / "Agent triaging". A capped kanban_external_cards
list overrode count stamps, so a down card outside the 10 listed painted no red. The
hollow cloud was a data attribute with no style and ignored client-derived unknown.
Down-only dots were titled "Running on an external service".

Proof: tests failed on 2da5291b (11), then 159 passed on this tree. tsc --noEmit,
eslint on touched files, and scripts/check --only health --base origin/main are clean.

Co-Authored-By: Grok 4.6 <noreply@x.ai>
